        <h2>The Challenge</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="row justify-content-center" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100" data-aos-duration="500">
        <div class="col-md-12 col-lg-10 text-center">
          <p>Healthcare institutions in Bihar face systemic challenges that significantly hinder their ability to deliver quality services efficiently. Fragmented departmental structures lead to inefficiencies, while limited awareness and understanding of Key Responsibility Areas (KRAs) and Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) restrict accountability and efficiency.</p>
          <p>Weak decision-making frameworks (RACI, PESTLE, etc.) contribute to governance gaps, and inadequate onboarding and training for new staff affect service quality. These challenges are further exacerbated by deeply entrenched institutional mindsets and rigid governance frameworks that resist change. For example, District Hospital Departments manage over 43 registers, causing delays and data duplication. The grievance resolution mechanism requires patient-centric interfaces. The OD Centre of Excellence (OD CoE) addresses these challenges through diagnostic assessments, development, designing and deploying context-specific solutions, structured onboarding, and performance-tracking tools such as the Sewa Bhaav Readiness Assessment, Sewa Atlas Pathways that Map Vulnerabilities, and Guiding Services. The OD CoE nurtures a culture of accountability, collaboration, and citizen engagement across healthcare institutions.</p>
